[Event "QGD: 4.Bg5 (Tartakower)"]

{Black holds d5 with ...e6, castles, and frees the position with ...b6 and ...Bb7, or with ...c5.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.}
1... d5 {Black matches.}
2. c4 {[%cal Gc4d5] The Queen's Gambit.}
2... e6 {[%cal Ge6d5] Declined. Black holds d5.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Development.}
4. Bg5 {[%cal Gg5f6] Pins.}
(4. Bf4 {Development.}
 4... Be7 {Development.}
 5. e3 {Solid.}
 5... O-O {Castles.}
 6. Nf3 {Development.}
 6... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
 7. dxc5 {Captures.}
 7... Bxc5 {Recaptures.})
4... Be7 {Breaks the pin.}
5. e3 {Solid.}
(5. Nf3 {Development.}
 5... h6 {Questions the bishop.}
 6. Bh4 {Keeps the pin.}
 6... O-O {Castles.}
 7. e3 {Solid.}
 7... b6 {The Tartakower.})
5... O-O {Castles.}
6. Nf3 {Development.}
6... h6 {Questions the bishop.}
7. Bh4 {Keeps the pin.}
7... b6 {[%cal Gc8b7] The Tartakower. It prepares ...Bb7.}
8. Be2 {Development.}
8... Bb7 {Development.}
9. Bxf6 {Trades.}
9... Bxf6 {Recaptures.}
10. cxd5 {Captures.}
10... exd5 {[%cal Gb7d5] Recaptures. The pawn on d5 is solid.} *

[Event "QGD: Exchange"]

{In the Carlsbad structure, White often plays a minority attack with b4 and b5.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.}
1... d5 {Black matches.}
2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit.}
2... e6 {Declined.}
3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5.}
3... Nf6 {Development.}
4. cxd5 {The Exchange.}
4... exd5 {[%cal Gc8f5] Recaptures, opening the bishop.}
5. Bg5 {Pins.}
5... c6 {Solid.}
6. e3 {Solid.}
6... Be7 {Development.}
7. Bd3 {Development.}
7... Nbd7 {Development.}
8. Qc2 {[%cal Gc2h7] Aims at h7.}
8... O-O {Castles.}
9. Nge2 {Development.}
9... Re8 {Development.} *

[Event "QGD: 3.Nf3 / Catalan"]

{The Catalan: the g2-bishop pressures the queenside. Black often takes on c4 and holds the pawn for a while.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.}
1... d5 {Black matches.}
2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit.}
2... e6 {Declined.}
3. Nf3 {Development.}
3... Nf6 {Development.}
4. g3 {[%cal Gf1g2] The Catalan.}
(4. Nc3 {Development.}
 4... Be7 {Development.}
 5. Bf4 {Development.}
 5... O-O {Castles.}
 6. e3 {Solid.}
 6... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
 7. dxc5 {Captures.}
 7... Bxc5 {Recaptures.}
 8. Qc2 {Development.}
 8... Nc6 {Development.})
4... Be7 {Development.}
5. Bg2 {Fianchetto.}
5... O-O {Castles.}
6. O-O {King safety.}
6... dxc4 {Takes the pawn.}
7. Qc2 {Prepares to regain c4.}
7... a6 {Prepares ...b5.}
8. Qxc4 {Regains the pawn.}
8... b5 {Gains space with tempo.}
9. Qc2 {Retreats.}
9... Bb7 {[%cal Gb7g2] Contests the diagonal.} *

[Event "QGD vs London"]

{Against the London, Black plays ...c5 and ...Nc6 to put pressure on d4 and b2.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.}
1... d5 {Black matches.}
2. Bf4 {The London.}
2... Nf6 {Development.}
3. e3 {Solid.}
3... e6 {Solid.}
4. Nf3 {Development.}
4... c5 {Strikes at d4.}
5. c3 {Holds d4.}
5... Nc6 {Pressure on d4.}
6. Nbd2 {Development.}
6... Bd6 {[%cal Gd6f4] Challenges the f4-bishop.}
7. Bg3 {Keeps it.}
7... O-O {Castles.} *

[Event "QGD: Elephant Trap"]

{The trap: after 4...Nbd7, 5.cxd5 exd5 6.Nxd5?? loses to 6...Nxd5! 7.Bxd8 Bb4+ 8.Qd2 Bxd2+ 9.Kxd2 Kxd8, and Black is a piece up.}
1. d4 {Takes the centre.} 1... d5 {Black matches.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit.} 2... e6 {Declined.} 3. Nc3 {Pressure on d5.} 3... Nf6 {Development.} 4. Bg5 {Pins the knight.} 4... Nbd7 {[%csl Gd8] Looks like it leaves d5 loose, but it sets the trap.}
5. cxd5 {Captures.}
5... exd5 {Recaptures.}
6. Nxd5?? {[%cal Gd5f6] White grabs a pawn because the f6-knight is pinned... or so it seems.}
6... Nxd5! {[%cal Gd5d8] Gives up the queen!}
7. Bxd8 {Takes the queen.}
7... Bb4+ {[%cal Gb4e1] Check.}
8. Qd2 {The only move.}
8... Bxd2+ {Takes the queen.}
9. Kxd2 {Recaptures.}
9... Kxd8 {Black is a piece up.} *
